 61MN c  Compiled by A. MacDonald and B. Singh (McMaster); May 21, 2009.        
 61MN c  {+61}Cr produced through the {+9}Be({+76}Ge,X) reaction at a beam      
 61MN2c  energy of 130 MeV/nucleon. The {+76}Ge beam was produced by the        
 61MN3c  coupled cyclotrons at the National Superconducting Cyclotron           
 61MN4c  Laboratory at Michigan State University. Fragments were separated      
 61MN5c  using the A1900 fragment separator. The |b's and |g's were measured    
 61MN6c  using the Beta Counting System and the Segmented Germanium Array, as   
 61MN7c  well as three Si PIN detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b, |b|g coin,
 61MN8c  (fragmnent)|b coin, half-life of the {+61}Cr ground state.             
 61MN c  Fragments identified: {+57}Sc, {+58}Ti, {+59}Ti, {+59}V, {+60}V,       
 61MN2c  {+60}Cr, {+61}Cr, {+62}Cr, {+62}Mn, {+63}Mn                            
